            "answer": {
              "short": "First branches: R, B, W. Second branches: B and W after R; R and W after B; R and B after W.",
              "worked": "Let R, B and W denote red, blue and white. Each first branch has two second branches because the first marble is not replaced. There are $3\\times2=6$ equally likely paths.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 70
          },
          {
            "id": "p15-q18-b",
            "type": "part",
