            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{2}{3}$",
              "worked": "The favourable outcomes are RB, RW, BR and WR. Two red marbles are impossible.\n$P(\\text{at least one red})=\\frac{4}{6}=\\frac{2}{3}$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 22
          },
